round knowledge and the default-state-presence rule.","unit":"CD8309-lubefu","run_id":"drc-swarm-1"},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Lubefu centre (Jerico / Lubefu Mission), territorial seat","evidence":"Seat of the territorial administration with a PNC commissariat; Lubefu lies far from the eastern conflict zones and outside armed-group territorial control. Live web research was unavailable for this run (web search budget exhausted, Wikipedia blocked by the egress proxy), so this rests on background knowledge and the default-state-presence rule.","unit":"CD8309-lubefu","run_id":"drc-swarm-1"},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Tshumbe (Tshumbe Mission / Dihokalenge agglomeration), Dikungu secteur","evidence":"Tshumbe is the largest town of Lubefu territory and seat of the Catholic diocese, with a PNC presence, courts and territorial services; no armed group is known to hold or tax it. Insecurity is limited to banditry and political/customary tensions. Live web research was unavailable for this run (web search budget exhausted, Wikipedia blocked by the egress proxy), so this rests on background knowledge and the default-state-presence rule.","unit":"CD8309-lubefu","run_id":"drc-swarm-1"}],"sources":{},"units":{"CD8309-lubefu":"Lubefu territory (Sankuru) covers the Dikungu, Minga and Tshumbe secteurs, with Tshumbe (diocesan centre) as its largest town and Lubefu as territorial seat. It lies far from the eastern conflict zones and outside the core Kamuina Nsapu theatre; no armed group is known to hold territory as of 2026. Insecurity is mainly banditry, political tension and customary/land disputes. All locations are assessed as under ordinary state authority with the PNC as the main permanent force. Live web research was unavailable for this run, so confidence is medium for the towns and low for rural areas."}}